description: PHPDoc for Aheadworks PHP — methods only, no @inheritdoc, simple @param types
globs: app/code/Aheadworks/**/*.php
alwaysApply: false
---

# Aheadworks PHPDoc

## Methods (interface and implementation)

Every public/protected/private method must have a real PHPDoc: short description + `@param` / `@return` / `@throws` as needed. **`@inheritdoc` is forbidden.**

```php
/**
 * Get Preview
 *
 * @param int $id
 * @return array
 */
public function getPreview(int $id): array
```

### `__construct`

Document **parameters only** — no method summary line.

```php
/**
 * @param Context $context
 * @param ShippingClassRepositoryInterface $shippingClassRepository
 */
public function __construct(
    Context $context,
    private readonly ShippingClassRepositoryInterface $shippingClassRepository
) {
```

### `@param` types

Keep types simple. Do **not** use nested generics / shaped arrays.

```php
// ❌
@param array<int, array<string, string>> $res

// ✅
@param array $res
```

## Classes

Do **not** add a class-level docblock by default. Document **methods**, not the class.

```php
// ❌
/**
 * Save shipping class controller.
 */
class Save extends ShippingClass

// ✅
class Save extends ShippingClass
```

Add a class docblock only in rare cases when the class itself holds non-obvious complex logic that methods alone cannot explain.
